> Is there some trick to get the priest to gradually step
> farther and farther away from the altar?  Anything I've tried
> with a priest to block his way ends up with him stalled in
> a square adjacent to the altar.

It's almost impossible to maneuvre a peaceful cleric away from the
altar s/he's tending. It's probably easier (but also much more
hazardous) to anger the cleric and put her/him to sleep while a few
steps away from the altar before blocking the way back.

My favourite odd trick: 
If you're 'skilled' in polearms, you can stand a knight's move away
from the throne room door in Ludios and whack away with your weapon;
only the dragons can get at you, most foes are completely unable to
attack you. You don't even need a lamp because the door square is
always lit. 

If you have a moat and wands of both cold and fire, you can create ice
bridges, lure nasty monsters on them and shoot the ice away with a
fire blast - instant kill via drowning. I've used that trick more than
once against Croesus.

